      "message": "\u003e I still think the name of this method is misleading. What this signifies is the amount of space that needs to be allocated *above and beyond* what allocateSpace managed to allocate, right ? In other words, this is a signal for the amount of space that needs to be freed.\n\nIt is the total amount of space needed. To be more specific, this always return the same number X no matter how much free space is on the device, as long as total free space on the device \u003c X. This is NOT space that needs to be allocated *above and beyond* what allocateSpace allocates.\n\nDoes that align with the name \u0026 Javadoc you suggest?",
